'''Concordia International Airport''' ({{lang-bl|Aeroporto Internacional de Concordia}}), commonly known as '''Castejón Airport''', '''Castejón-Concordia Airport''', and '''Castejón International Airport''' {{Airport codes|CNX|SHCO}}, is one of the two airports that serves the surrounding [[Concordia|eponymous conurbation]], and is the primary base of [[Balisca]]'s major domestic airline, [[Baliscana]] (Terminal 1). It is located in the [[La Joya]] canton in [[Luzamontaña]], bordering southwest [[Castejón]]. It co-shares runway facilities with the military airport of the [[La Joya Air Base]], primarily runways three and four.

Prior to it's the airport's construction Castejón was served by [[Alunzaro International Airport|Alunzaro Airport]], which was built in 1953 to serve the city of [[Jatiel]]. Concordia has been the primary international airport serving the conurbation since 1978, handling almost all of its domestic flights. Concordia underwent significant renovation between 2012 and 2014: a dedicated International Terminal, current Terminal 3, was opened at Concordia in conjunction with the completion of a fourth runway, allowing increased long-haul flights during night-time hours. The communal government is currently encouraging the use of Concordia for premium business routes and the use of the smaller [[Rincónoro Airport]] for domestic and regional leisure routes and by low-cost carriers.

Concordia handled 60,278,809 passengers in 2019; by passenger throughput, it was the [[List of busiest airports in Abyala|busiest airport in Abyala]] and the [[List of busiest airports in Adonia by passenger traffic|Xth-busiest in Adonia]]. It is able to handle 75 million passengers per year, following renovations in 2018. 

